        <mxCell id="p0c155" value="&lt;b&gt;How to read it&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Glidepaths feed four tables that together decide 7 visuals (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8).&lt;br&gt;Loss Units (Volume Loss Correction) decide 6 visuals (2, 3, 5, 7, 8, 9).&lt;br&gt;Machine Names (13 visuals) and Plan OPT (9) are the base of the page and are mostly complete.&lt;br&gt;Format List and Equipment Coding matter on other report pages (By Format, Maintenance), not on this page." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1600" y="1072" width="700" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sep-p0c156" value="&lt;b&gt;Table separation for eu_report (decided 2026-10-15)&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=14;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2400" y="170" width="900" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sep-p0c157" value="&lt;b&gt;Folders in the data lake: eu_report/ih_report, eu_report/pbi_report, eu_report/reference&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;ih_report = end goal: Insights Hub data enriched with the reference files.&lt;br&gt;pbi_report = the data we have now (Provideam exports), so Reckitt can see the dashboard with their own data.&lt;br&gt;Both hold the same 6 tables in the Power BI shape. Only the source differs. The old reports folder stays." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2400" y="200" width="900" height="104" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
