        <mxCell id="p4c136" value="&lt;b&gt;ASSUMPTION + PARTLY FILLED 73%&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Assumption: design speed x duration. The rule is the same as in the Provideam files: loss units per minute = capacity per planned minute (Nottingham: 2,341 of 2,349 machine-days within 3%). The report reads the units from the Volume Loss Correction file. See the sheet Explanation Loss Units." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=4;fontSize=10.5;" parent="1" vertex="1">
