        <mxCell id="p13c87" value="&lt;b&gt;Independent of both&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1230" y="972" width="330" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13c88" value="&lt;b&gt;What this means for replacing Provideam&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1038" width="1500" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p13c89" value="1. Overlap rows: Insights Hub can supply the data, but the numbers differ. On the overlap days the Insights Hub good parts are 96.6% (B2) and 43.6% (GT4) of the Provideam good parts. Reckitt must name the official source per site.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;2. Only Provideam: we need the Provideam files or the Provideam rules. Or Reckitt accepts that the column is empty (for example comment text).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;3. Excel files: they do not depend on the OEE source. We need them in every case.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;4. At a switch, the history in the report changes: Provideam numbers before the date, Insights Hub numbers after it." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=8;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1072" width="1520" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
