        <mxCell id="p14c78" value="&lt;b&gt;Open decisions and blockers&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1194" width="1500" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p14c79" value="1. Official OEE source per site, today and after the move (Provideam or Insights Hub). Question for Mei Shin and Asif.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;2. Machine key: asset ID or machine name + site. All mapping tables depend on it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;3. Who builds the Power Automate flow, and the VFC receiver: file size limit and key handling are not tested.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;4. Access: Hull folders Equipment Coding, Line Losses, Machine Names, Packing Run Rates, Volume Loss Correction; the whole Mira site.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;5. File format for the integration: Provideam files are UTF-16 with tab separation, CR line ends, a Total row and comments with unescaped quotes. Ask for a clean export." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=8;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1228" width="1520" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram name="Explanation Plan to get the missing data" id="page-plan">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="p15c2" value="&lt;b&gt;Plan to get the missing data into the data lake: three options&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=18;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="20" width="1500" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c3" value="Why: Insights Hub has no data for targets, product formats, shift names, machine groups and equipment. The Power BI report gets them from SharePoint files. Status 2026-10-14. Files seen: Hull (partly), Nottingham, Weinheim. Mira: no access. Chartres, NMD and Tuzla: not checked. This sheet is for the decision with Asif." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="62" width="1520" height="74" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c4" value="&lt;b&gt;1 What must be collected&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="150" width="1500" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c5" value="&lt;b&gt;Class A: reference files (small, change rarely)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Glidepaths (4 files, 12 to 69 KB), Format Mapping (3 files, 3 to 15 KB), Shift Pattern (1 file, 5 KB), Machine Names (per site, 16 to 18 KB), Equipment Coding (per site, 8 to 265 KB).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Kept by hand by the sites. Glidepaths change monthly or yearly (the 2027 targets are still empty). Needed in every case, whatever the OEE source is." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="184" width="750" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c6" value="&lt;b&gt;Class B: Provideam report files (large, rewritten every hour)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Plan OPT, Line Losses, Run Rates, Volume Loss Correction: one file per month plus the current month, 17 KB to 6.5 MB each.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Needed only if Provideam data is kept next to Insights Hub (to compare or to migrate). Not needed if Insights Hub is the official source: this decision is open." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="810" y="184" width="750" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c7" value="&lt;b&gt;2 Three options (numbers as in our earlier discussion)&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="370" width="1500" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c8" value="&lt;b&gt;1  Power Automate sends the files&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="404" width="480" height="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c9" value="&lt;b&gt;How it works&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A flow of Reckitt runs when a file is created or changed in the SharePoint folder. It sends the file by HTTP POST to an endpoint of our VFC (http in node). The VFC converts the file and writes parquet to the data lake. Reckitt already runs Power Automate flows for these reports (maintenance guide)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="464" width="480" height="156" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c10" value="&lt;b&gt;What Reckitt must do&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A person at Reckitt builds and owns one flow per file type. We build and own the VFC receiver and give them the endpoint address and key (never in documents)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="628" width="480" height="104" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c11" value="&lt;b&gt;Tested?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;NOT tested. To check: size limit and body format of the VFC http in node, UTF-16 files, key handling, and whether the HTTP action of Power Automate needs a premium licence." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="740" width="480" height="104" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c12" value="&lt;b&gt;Good&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Push on change, no polling. No new access to SharePoint for us. A tool Reckitt already knows. One receiver serves all sites." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="852" width="480" height="96" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c13" value="&lt;b&gt;Risks&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A flow can fail without anyone noticing: we need a heartbeat check in our log. Large files (up to 6.5 MB) may exceed the limit. Reckitt must keep the flow alive. The key is a secret inside their flow." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="956" width="480" height="126" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c14" value="&lt;b&gt;2  Direct access: the VFC reads SharePoint&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="560" y="404" width="480" height="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c15" value="&lt;b&gt;How it works&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The VFC calls Microsoft Graph (or the SharePoint REST API) on a schedule, lists the folders, downloads new or changed files, converts them and writes parquet to the lake. It logs in with an app registration or a service account with read access to the folders." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="560" y="464" width="480" height="156" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c16" value="&lt;b&gt;What Reckitt must do&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Reckitt IT creates the app registration or service account and gives read access to the folders of all sites. We keep the secret in the Config node. The VFC must be allowed to call the Microsoft hosts." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="560" y="628" width="480" height="104" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c17" value="&lt;b&gt;Tested?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;NOT tested. To check: can the VFC reach the Microsoft login and Graph hosts, token handling in an http request node, and how long the IT approval takes." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="560" y="740" width="480" height="104" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c18" value="&lt;b&gt;Good&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fully in our control: schedule, retries, file history, logs. Nothing for Reckitt to maintain after the setup. One setup works for all sites." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="560" y="852" width="480" height="96" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c19" value="&lt;b&gt;Risks&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;IT approval is probably the slowest step. A secret that can read SharePoint must be kept safe and renewed. The permission scope may be wider than we need." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="560" y="956" width="480" height="126" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c20" value="&lt;b&gt;3  Manual copy (interim, works now)&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="404" width="480" height="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c21" value="&lt;b&gt;How it works&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The user downloads the files from SharePoint (browser, or Claude in Chrome) into the project folder. A script converts them (the loader is not built yet). The user puts the converted files into the data lake. First run: 36 files from the Nottingham site on 2026-10-14." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="464" width="480" height="156" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c22" value="&lt;b&gt;What Reckitt must do&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Access to each folder. Missing: five Hull folders and the whole Mira site." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="628" width="480" height="104" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c23" value="&lt;b&gt;Tested?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;TESTED and working on 2026-10-14: 36 files, all complete. Chrome blocks repeated automatic downloads, so real clicks are needed." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="740" width="480" height="104" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c24" value="&lt;b&gt;Good&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;No dependency on Reckitt IT. Good enough for Class A (small files, rare changes). Starts today." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="852" width="480" height="96" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c25" value="&lt;b&gt;Risks&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Manual work and delay. Class B files change every hour and go stale. Someone must remember to repeat it. Risk of an old file version: keep the download date in the file name." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="956" width="480" height="126" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c26" value="&lt;b&gt;3 Which option fits which class&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1110" width="1500" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c27" value="&lt;b&gt;Class A: reference files&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1146" width="700" height="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c28" value="Good fit. Small files, a push on change is enough." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1168" width="480" height="56" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c29" value="Works, but heavy for 5 small files that change rarely." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="560" y="1168" width="480" height="56" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c30" value="Good fit now. Enough while the files change rarely." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="1168" width="480" height="56" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c31" value="&lt;b&gt;Class B: Provideam report files&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1242" width="700" height="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c32" value="Possible. Size limit to test, and a push every hour." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1264" width="480" height="56" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c33" value="Best fit: schedule, history, large files." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="560" y="1264" width="480" height="56" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c34" value="Poor fit. The files go stale within hours." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="1264" width="480" height="56" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c35" value="&lt;b&gt;4 Recommended sequence&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1350" width="1500" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c36" value="&lt;b&gt;1 Now&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Manual copy of Class A for Hull, Nottingham and Weinheim (36 files done). Request the missing access: five Hull folders and the Mira site." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1384" width="290" height="132" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c37" value="&lt;b&gt;2 Small test&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Power Automate sends ONE small file (for example the Weinheim Glidepath, 12 KB) to a test endpoint in the VFC. It answers: size, key, UTF-16, licence." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="346" y="1384" width="290" height="132" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c38" value="&lt;b&gt;3 In parallel&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ask Reckitt IT if an app registration or a service account is possible (option 2)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="652" y="1384" width="290" height="132" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c39" value="&lt;b&gt;4 Decide&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Per class: Class A by option 1 or 2, or stay manual. Class B only if Provideam data is kept." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="958" y="1384" width="290" height="132" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c40" value="&lt;b&gt;5 Roll out&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;All 7 sites from one site list. A missing or late file shows in a report after each run." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#eeeeee;strokeColor=#999999;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1264" y="1384" width="290" height="132" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c41" value="&lt;b&gt;5 Decisions and help needed from Reckitt&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1546" width="1500" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c42" value="1. Which option for Class A: Power Automate, direct access, or manual for now.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;2. Who at Reckitt builds and owns the Power Automate flow.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;3. A contact in Reckitt IT for an app registration or a service account.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;4. The official OEE source per site (decides whether Class B is needed).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;5. Access: five Hull folders, the Mira site, and the files of Chartres, NMD and Tuzla (not seen yet)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;fontSize=11;arcSize=8;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10.5;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1580" width="1520" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c43" value="&lt;b&gt;6 Which missing data first: ranked by the visuals it affects (EU-Level Overview page, Segun lineage)&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1760" width="1500" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c44" value="&lt;b&gt;Missing data&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1796" width="430" height="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c45" value="&lt;b&gt;Visuals affected&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="480" y="1796" width="390" height="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p15c46" value="&lt;b&gt;Count&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="880" y="1796" width="90" height="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
